Vendored modules — attribution
==============================

The Python files in this directory are verbatim copies of modules
originally written for the Atlas research codebase, redistributed here so
that the public reproduction package is self-contained.

Source: the (private) Atlas research codebase.
Vendored files (only the three modules the repro pipeline actually uses):
  embed.py    -- Takens delay embedding + AMI/FNN parameter selection
  diffuse.py  -- diffusion maps (dense + Nystrom)
  config.py   -- EmbedConfig / DmapConfig dataclasses needed by the above

Copyright (c) Maximilian Topel; redistributed under the MIT license of the
parent this repository:  package (see ../../LICENSE).

These modules depend only on numpy / scipy / sklearn / POT / matplotlib /
joblib / ripser (already listed in this repository: requirements.txt). The
vendored config.py is needed for the `from config import ...` statements
inside the other vendored modules; `aoa_repro.config.use_vendor()` adds
this directory to sys.path so those imports resolve.

If the Atlas modules are subsequently published as a standalone package,
this directory should be replaced with an ordinary dependency declaration
in requirements.txt and the local files removed.
